item in possession.
Code:
//change in start
this._maxItemCount = $gameParty.numItems(item);

//to
this._maxItemCount = $gameParty.numItems(item) > 0;

//or

this._maxItemCount = $gameParty.numItems(item)>= 1;
see if that works.

In my opinion, the author did a mistake in this code section:
Code:
Scene_Item.prototype.modifyItemWindow = function(){
    this._itemWindow.isCurrentItemEnabled = function(){
        return true;
    }
}
This code means that you can open the menu on every item (which is correct), but ALSO when the item that you are clicking is blank (which is not correct, obviously).
Try replacing this section with this:
Code:
Scene_Item.prototype.modifyItemWindow = function(){
    this._itemWindow.isCurrentItemEnabled = function(){
        return !!this.item();
    }
}

I didn't know that, but you might be able to change this one too.
JavaScript:
Window_DiscardCount.prototype.isCancelEnabled = function() {
    return true;
}

//to (if working

Window_DiscardCount.prototype.isCancelEnabled = function() {
    if (this.item()?.meta["avoid"]) return false
    return true;
})
you can change "avoid" to avoid being discard if the item has any.
else, return true as if doesn't has any.
